{
  "scopeName": "ramonda.css-block",
  "injectionSelector": "L:meta.tag.tsx -meta.jsx.children -string -comment, L:meta.tag.jsx -meta.jsx.children -string -comment, L:meta.tag.ts -meta.jsx.children -string -comment, L:meta.tag.js -meta.jsx.children -string -comment",
  "patterns": [
    {
      "include": "#block"
    }
  ],
  "repository": {
    "block": {
      "begin": "(?<=\\s)([\\w:$-]+)\\s*(=)\\s*(@@)(\\()",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "entity.other.attribute-name"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "keyword.operator.assignment"
        },
        "3": {
          "name": "keyword.control.ramonda"
        },
        "4": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.begin.ramonda"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\\))",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.end.ramonda"
        }
      },
      "contentName": "meta.embedded.block.css",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#innards"
        }
      ],
      "comment": "The lookbehind mirrors the compiler's own scanner, which requires whitespace before the name. This pattern is only the BARE attribute form, where the name and the `=` are coloured too; a block in expression position is `ramonda.css-value`. The `@@` is this language's MARKER and is coloured as one wherever it appears. It opens a BLOCK and nothing else does: `when $( … )` and `...$( … )` carry no `@@`, because inside a block the language is the block's own. A user reported the two characters coming out as punctuation in one place and a keyword in another, which is a reader having to learn that the same marker means two things. The BRACKET keeps `punctuation.section.embedded.begin`, and that is not cosmetic: it is what pairs with the `contentName` an editor reads to treat the inside as CSS."
    },
    "innards": {
      "comment": "Order is the whole of it. A hole is ONE brace, and so is a nested rule's body — so every pattern that can recognise a hole from its POSITION runs before `#nested`, which would otherwise read `color: ` as a selector and the hole as a rule list. Measured: it did exactly that, and the CSS grammar agreed with it, scoping `accent` as a property name.",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#composition"
        },
        {
          "include": "#block-match"
        },
        {
          "include": "#hole-in-a-name"
        },
        {
          "include": "#declaration-with-a-match"
        },
        {
          "include": "#nested"
        },
        {
          "include": "#group"
        },
        {
          "include": "source.css#rule-list-innards"
        }
      ]
    },
    "nested": {
      "comment": "A nested rule. The editor's CSS grammar has no pattern for one — measured, `&:hover {` comes back as a property whose value is `hover {` — so the block handles nesting itself. It runs LAST among the brace patterns: everything that can tell a hole by its position has already had the line, so a `{` reaching here opens a rule.",
      "begin": "([^;{}]+?)(\\{)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "patterns": [
            {
              "comment": "`&` is CSS nesting's own, and the editor's CSS grammar has no pattern for it either.",
              "match": "&",
              "name": "entity.other.attribute-name.parent-selector.css"
            },
            {
              "include": "source.css#selector-innards"
            }
          ]
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.property-list.begin.bracket.curly.css"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\\})",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.property-list.end.bracket.curly.css"
        }
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#innards"
        }
      ]
    },
    "composition": {
      "comment": "The block's own words: `when $( … )`, `else when $( … )`, a bare `else`, and `...$( … )`. Each is a keyword and each escape is TypeScript; the `{ … }` that follows a condition is an ordinary group, read by `nested` or `group`.",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "begin": "\\s*\\b(?:(else)\\s+)?(when)\\s*(\\$)(\\()",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "keyword.control.ramonda"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "keyword.control.ramonda"
            },
            "3": {
              "name": "keyword.control.ramonda"
            },
            "4": {
              "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.begin.ramonda"
            }
          },
          "end": "(\\))",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.end.ramonda"
            }
          },
          "contentName": "meta.embedded.expression.tsx",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "source.tsx"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "match": "\\s*\\b(else)\\b(?=\\s*\\{)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "keyword.control.ramonda"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "begin": "\\s*(\\.\\.\\.)\\s*(\\$)(\\()",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "keyword.control.ramonda"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "keyword.control.ramonda"
            },
            "3": {
              "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.begin.ramonda"
            }
          },
          "end": "(\\))",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.end.ramonda"
            }
          },
          "contentName": "meta.embedded.expression.tsx",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "source.tsx"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "hole-in-a-name": {
      "comment": "`$(angle): 45deg` — an escape where a property name goes, which is how a registered property is set.",
      "begin": "\\s*(\\$)(\\()(?=[^()]*\\)\\s*:)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "keyword.control.ramonda"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.begin.ramonda"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\\))",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.end.ramonda"
        }
      },
      "contentName": "meta.embedded.expression.tsx",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "source.tsx"
        }
      ]
    },
    "block-match": {
      "comment": "`match $( … ) { key => ( … ); … }` at the head of an item: the word, its subject, and the arms inside the braces.",
      "begin": "\\s*\\b(match)(?=\\s*\\$\\()",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "keyword.control.ramonda"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\\})",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.property-list.end.bracket.curly.css"
        }
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "comment": "The subject.",
          "begin": "(\\$)(\\()",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "keyword.control.ramonda"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.begin.ramonda"
            }
          },
          "end": "(\\))",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.end.ramonda"
            }
          },
          "contentName": "meta.embedded.expression.tsx",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "source.tsx"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "match": "(\\{)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.section.property-list.begin.bracket.curly.css"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "include": "source.css#comment-block"
        },
        {
          "comment": "One arm, `key => ( … );` — the key, the arrow, and the declarations it applies, read as any group's are.",
          "begin": "\\s*([^\\s=;{}()][^=;{}()]*?)\\s*(=>)\\s*(\\()",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "constant.other.key.ramonda"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "keyword.operator.ramonda"
            },
            "3": {
              "name": "punctuation.section.arm.begin.ramonda"
            }
          },
          "end": "(\\))\\s*(;)?",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.section.arm.end.ramonda"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "punctuation.terminator.rule.css"
            }
          },
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#innards"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "declaration-with-a-match": {
      "comment": "A declaration whose value is a `match` — the one value that holds braces, so without this the CSS grammar reads `color: match $(t) {` as a nested rule's selector.",
      "begin": "(?=\\s*(?:--)?[-\\w]+\\s*:\\s*match\\s*\\$\\()\\s*((?:--)?[-\\w]+)\\s*(:)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "support.type.property-name.css"
        },
        "2": {
          "name": "punctuation.separator.key-value.css"
        }
      },
      "end": "(;)|(?=\\})",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.terminator.rule.css"
        }
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "begin": "\\b(match)(?=\\s*\\$\\()",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "keyword.control.ramonda"
            }
          },
          "end": "(\\})",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.section.match.end.ramonda"
            }
          },
          "patterns": [
            {
              "comment": "The subject.",
              "begin": "(\\$)(\\()",
              "beginCaptures": {
                "1": {
                  "name": "keyword.control.ramonda"
                },
                "2": {
                  "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.begin.ramonda"
                }
              },
              "end": "(\\))",
              "endCaptures": {
                "1": {
                  "name": "punctuation.section.embedded.end.ramonda"
                }
              },
              "contentName": "meta.embedded.expression.tsx",
              "patterns": [
                {
                  "include": "source.tsx"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "match": "(\\{)",
              "captures": {
                "1": {
                  "name": "punctuation.section.match.begin.ramonda"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "match": "(=>)",
              "captures": {
                "1": {
                  "name": "keyword.operator.ramonda"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "match": "(;)",
              "captures": {
                "1": {
                  "name": "punctuation.terminator.arm.ramonda"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "include": "ramonda.css-variable#variable"
            },
            {
              "include": "source.css#property-values"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "group": {
      "comment": "A `{ … }` with nothing in front of it on the line — the body after `when $( … )`, `else` or `} else`, written tight.",
      "begin": "(\\{)",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.property-list.begin.bracket.curly.css"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\\})",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.section.property-list.end.bracket.curly.css"
        }
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#innards"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
